<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuruc</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1671–1711</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Kurucs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuruc was the name given to the armed anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rebels of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-hungary">Royal Hungary</a> between 1671 and 1711. Drawn from Protestant nobles, lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a>, haiduks and peasants, they fought against Habsburg absolutism and religious persecution, first under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imre-thokoly">Imre Thököly</a> and later in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi">Francis II Rákóczi</a>'s War of Independence, which ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-szatmar">Peace of Szatmár</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kuruc.jpg" alt="Kuruc" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Viktor Madarász · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madar%C3%A1sz_Kuruc_%C3%A9s_labanc_1855.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
